drm/amd/display: hold the VRR vblank reference only while a CRTC is on

amdgpu_dm_handle_vrr_transition() takes a vblank reference when a
CRTC's VRR goes from inactive to active and gives it back on the way
down, judging only the freesync config. An inactive CRTC can carry an
active config, and then the reference is asked for while its vblank is
off. On an 8 GiB Surface Laptop 4, every wake after a screen was
switched off before suspend warned:

  WARNING: drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/../display/amdgpu_dm/
  amdgpu_dm_freesync.c:333 at amdgpu_dm_handle_vrr_transition+0x1cd
   amdgpu_dm_atomic_commit_tail+0x18d9/0x3a10 [amdgpu]
   drm_atomic_helper_commit_duplicated_state+0x155/0x170
   drm_atomic_helper_resume+0xca/0x170
   dm_resume+0xb7c/0xd10 [amdgpu]

dm_resume() commits the cached state through drm_atomic_helper_resume().
The CRTC that was switched off is still inactive in it, so
amdgpu_dm_atomic_commit_tail() doesn't call manage_dm_interrupts() for
it, but its freesync config there is active, so the transition sees VRR
go from off to on (amdgpu_dm_reset_freesync_config_for_crtc(), which
dm_destroy_cached_state() calls, leaves freesync_config.state as it
was). drm_crtc_vblank_get() finds the refcount held by
drm_crtc_vblank_off() and vblank disabled, and returns -EINVAL. The
capture with drm.debug shows it in order: drm_crtc_vblank_off on crtc 1
at 941.590 as the screen went off, the warning at 943.164 inside
dm_resume, and drm_crtc_vblank_on_config on crtc 1 only at 943.322, when
the compositor turned the screen back on. The failed get also leaves the
reference uncounted, so the next VRR on->off put gives back one it never
took.

Count VRR as active only while the CRTC state is active. A CRTC coming
on gets its reference after manage_dm_interrupts() has called
drm_crtc_vblank_on() earlier in the same loop; one going off puts it
after amdgpu_dm_commit_streams() has called drm_crtc_vblank_off(), whose
inmodeset reference keeps the count above zero. A modeset of a CRTC that
stays on keeps its reference as before. Mainline's "Fix vblank refcount
in vrr transition" (2022) fixed the order of these calls, not this case.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_freesync.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_freesync.c
@@ -313,8 +313,18 @@ void amdgpu_dm_handle_vrr_transition(str
 				     struct dm_crtc_state *new_state)
 {
 	struct amdgpu_device *adev = dm->adev;
-	bool old_vrr_active = amdgpu_dm_crtc_vrr_active(old_state);
-	bool new_vrr_active = amdgpu_dm_crtc_vrr_active(new_state);
+	/*
+	 * A CRTC holds its VRR vblank reference only while it is on. An
+	 * inactive CRTC can still carry an active freesync config, as when a
+	 * resume restores a CRTC that was off before suspend, and its vblank
+	 * is off, so drm_crtc_vblank_get() would fail. The reference is taken
+	 * once the CRTC comes on, after drm_crtc_vblank_on(), and given back
+	 * when it goes off, after drm_crtc_vblank_off().
+	 */
+	bool old_vrr_active = old_state->base.active &&
+			      amdgpu_dm_crtc_vrr_active(old_state);
+	bool new_vrr_active = new_state->base.active &&
+			      amdgpu_dm_crtc_vrr_active(new_state);
 
 	/* Only DCE gates vupdate on VRR, keep it enabled for DCN */
 	bool vrr_gates_vupdate = amdgpu_ip_version(adev, DCE_HWIP, 0) == 0;
